<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yaroslav Osmomysl</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1135–<a href="/years/1187">1187</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Yaroslav Volodymyrkovych</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yaroslav Osmomysl, meaning 'of eight minds', was Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> from 1153 to 1187, son of Volodymyrko. Under him Galicia reached the height of its power and prosperity, extending towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-tale-of-igors-campaign">Lay of Igor's Campaign</a> praised him as a mighty ruler.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yaroslav-osmomysl.jpg" alt="Yaroslav Osmomysl" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Радзивилловская летопись · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%A1%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%82_%D0%B3%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%86%D0%BA%D0%B8%D1%85_%D0%B1%D0%BE%D1%8F%D1%80_%D1%81_%D1%8E%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%BC_%D0%BA%D0%BD%D1%8F%D0%B7%D0%B5%D0%BC_%D0%AF%D1%80%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%BC_%D0%92%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B4%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D0%BC_%D0%93%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%86%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%BC_%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B8_%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%BB%D1%83%D1%87%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B8_%D0%B8%D0%B7%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B8%D1%8F_%D0%BE_%D0%BF%D0%BE%D1%85%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B5_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%93%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%87_%D0%98%D0%B7%D1%8F%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0_%D0%9C%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B8%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
